00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:20,320
<i>You sell a ton of books.
You're a huge success.</i>

237
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:23,000
<i>It's not an autobiography per se.</i>

238
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:26,840
<i>I can polish and distort things.
You do that too, don't you?</i>

239
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:29,080
<i>But we never lie.</i>

240
00:21:29,320 --> 00:21:33,800
<i>I wouldn't say I do.
But I can spice things up.</i>

241
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:37,400
<i>Do you have anxiety?</i>

242
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:42,000
<i>I don't have a diagnosis on paper,
but that's never interested me.</i>

243
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:45,440
<i>I know I have ADHD. I know that.</i>

244
00:21:45,600 --> 00:21:50,960
<i>And I have enormous anxiety.
It's my companion, my best friend.</i>

245
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:55,440
<i>Ultimately, I'm an insecure little boy
who wants everyone to like him.</i>

246
00:21:55,600 --> 00:21:59,280
<i>But I think that's universal.
Doesn't everyone want to be liked?</i>

247
00:22:19,720 --> 00:22:21,520
Where have you been?

248
00:22:24,440 --> 00:22:26,680
I just went power-walking.

249
00:22:27,640 --> 00:22:29,680
In the middle of the night?

250
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:36,120
When I had finished showering,
you were just lying here snoring.

251
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:40,000
I was all worked up, so I went for a walk.

252
00:22:40,480 --> 00:22:46,800
- You smell of smoke.
- Come on, I'm anxious. Okay?

253
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:50,600
It was that kind of a
walk, I just threw up.

254
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:55,760
But darling, then just say so.

255
00:22:57,760 --> 00:23:01,160
And you were super-horny too.

256
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:04,680
Come here, you poor thing.

257
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:10,840
Poor little poppy.

258
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:15,920
- I'm really tired now.
- Shh, come here.

259
00:23:17,080 --> 00:23:21,480
Just a quickie.
What do you say, darling?

260
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:29,200
You'll love it.

261
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:57,520
<i>One wants to be loved.</i>

262
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:01,160
<i>Failing that, admired.</i>

263
00:24:02,360 --> 00:24:05,440
<i>Failing that, feared.</i>

264
00:24:06,080 --> 00:24:10,600
<i>Failing that, hated and despised.</i>

265
00:24:11,720 --> 00:24:14,480
<i>One wants to inspire
some kind of feeling in people.</i>

266
00:24:15,560 --> 00:24:19,920
<i>The soul shudders at the void
and wants contact.</i>

267
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:22,520
<i>At any price.</i>

268
00:24:40,680 --> 00:24:42,440
- Good morning, Kristin.
- Good morning.

269
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:45,640
Do you have Helga Gregorius's number
in your system?

270
00:24:45,880 --> 00:24:48,000
I need to reschedule her appointment.

271
00:24:48,200 --> 00:24:51,040
I don't think I have her private number.

272
00:24:51,320 --> 00:24:54,400
- But you can probably ask now.
- Why?

273
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:11,920
A therapist used to be here.

274
00:25:13,120 --> 00:25:15,360
I wonder why Lena actually fired him.

275
00:25:18,560 --> 00:25:20,840
- Patrik.
- Gabriel Glas.

276
00:25:21,840 --> 00:25:26,000
- I've seen you before.
- You've probably seen me here?

277
00:25:27,800 --> 00:25:29,360
Probably.

278
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:36,040
- I'm surprised to see you.
- Why?

279
00:25:36,200 --> 00:25:41,200
I knew Lena had hired a new doctor,
but that he'd be so young...

280
00:25:42,800 --> 00:25:43,680
And inexperienced.

281
00:25:43,840 --> 00:25:47,720
I've been practicing for almost
two years.

282
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:52,440
- Are you stupid, then?
- No, I wouldn't say that.

283
00:25:53,800 --> 00:25:57,440
That makes this whole thing
even stranger, I think. Right?

284
00:25:57,600 --> 00:26:01,840
- What thing?
- What you prescribed.

285
00:26:03,840 --> 00:26:04,840
To my wife.

286
00:26:08,360 --> 00:26:12,320
- Sit down, and we can...
- No. What you did is malpractice.

287
00:26:12,480 --> 00:26:16,120
But before I go to Lena,
I want to hear what you have to say.

288
00:26:19,080 --> 00:26:25,000
- You mean what Helga said about you?
- Have you been talking about me?

289
00:26:26,360 --> 00:26:30,120
Did you prescribe painkillers and benzos
to Helga because of me?

290
00:26:31,600 --> 00:26:35,240
Sorry, I thought maybe you had talked,

291
00:26:35,560 --> 00:26:37,720
but I can't say,
I have a duty of confidentiality.

292
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:42,480
Helga is an addict. She lies to get pills.

293
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:44,440
I don't think she lied.

294
00:26:44,920 --> 00:26:46,240
What did she say, then?

295
00:26:47,160 --> 00:26:49,240
I can't say, I have a
duty of confidentiality.

296
00:26:49,520 --> 00:26:51,320
Then I'm going to Lena.

297
00:26:52,480 --> 00:26:54,160
"She loved him, only him."

298
00:26:54,320 --> 00:26:58,200
"But he couldn't love anything
that hadn't already passed."

299
00:26:59,640 --> 00:27:01,640
I wrote that.

300
00:27:03,480 --> 00:27:07,040
- Are you mocking me?
- On the contrary.

301
00:27:07,280 --> 00:27:10,720
I think about that sentence almost daily.

302
00:27:15,720 --> 00:27:19,080
Yeah, I like that sentence too.

303
00:27:22,360 --> 00:27:26,880
- Should we review things, maybe?
- Sit down.

304
00:27:36,560 --> 00:27:37,920
What did Helga say?

305
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:47,040
<i>Helga is disgusted by you. She hates you.</i>

306
00:27:49,040 --> 00:27:51,640
Helga is worried about you.

307
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:54,760
She thinks you seem stressed,

308
00:27:54,920 --> 00:27:58,760
and feels that you're heading into another
depression.

309
00:27:58,920 --> 00:28:00,680
- Did she say that?
- Yes.

310
00:28:00,840 --> 00:28:03,080
That she's worried about me?

311
00:28:03,440 --> 00:28:07,400
- She's not well. Back pain.
- That's bullshit.

312
00:28:07,560 --> 00:28:12,480
But it was because, she said,
your anxiety is so powerful

313
00:28:12,640 --> 00:28:15,480
that it spreads to her.

314
00:28:15,680 --> 00:28:19,520
Fuck, that's awful.
I didn't know it was that bad.

315
00:28:21,440 --> 00:28:27,160
Have you been feeling extra tired lately?
I mean the last week, specifically.

316
00:28:27,440 --> 00:28:30,640
Yeah, actually. Definitely.
Morning and night.

317
00:28:30,800 --> 00:28:35,280
- I'm completely wiped.
- Yeah. And your sex drive, how is that?

318
00:28:35,520 --> 00:28:40,040
No problems. Works perfectly.
I love fucking Helga.

319
00:28:40,200 --> 00:28:43,000
You've seen her yourself.
It's not that strange.

320
00:28:44,200 --> 00:28:45,760
That's not my focus here.

321
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:50,400
If I may be frank, you're showing
symptoms of depression, Patrik.

322
00:28:51,160 --> 00:28:53,320
Do you get feelings of panic?

323
00:28:54,160 --> 00:28:54,880
And anxiety.

324
00:28:56,400 --> 00:29:00,320
Maybe I just have control issues.

325
00:29:00,480 --> 00:29:04,760
Helga isn't an easy match. It's a
full-time job keeping an eye on her.

326
00:29:04,920 --> 00:29:08,760
I love her drive, but she's
hiding something. She lies to me.

327
00:29:09,880 --> 00:29:13,680
I pick up from daycare, I cook, pay bills.

328
00:29:13,840 --> 00:29:17,440
I'm going under.
But I didn't know it was that bad.

329
00:29:17,600 --> 00:29:20,560
That it was affecting
her. Did she say that?

330
00:29:21,400 --> 00:29:25,360
Listen to me, my mind
is all over the place.

331
00:29:25,720 --> 00:29:30,720
I see Lena has you
on a low dose of sertraline.

332
00:29:31,760 --> 00:29:32,880
What about it?

333
00:29:33,960 --> 00:29:35,520
No, I can't interfere.

334
00:29:35,680 --> 00:29:38,480
Lena is a psychiatrist,
one of the best in the country.

335
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:40,680
She's a bit old school, sure,

336
00:29:40,840 --> 00:29:43,360
but no, it would be like I'm trying to
steal her patient.

337
00:29:43,520 --> 00:29:45,280
Forget it. So, what would you do?

338
00:29:47,520 --> 00:29:48,800
Say it!

339
00:29:51,440 --> 00:29:54,600
- If I were your patient.
- Yeah...

340
00:29:59,320 --> 00:30:02,880
Great. I knew there was
a reason I came here today.

341
00:30:03,040 --> 00:30:06,640
And then, Gabriel, I was thinking...
No, forget it.

342
00:30:06,800 --> 00:30:10,240
Lena! Really great guy.
See you. I have to run.

343
00:30:10,400 --> 00:30:13,000
- Bye.
- Bye, Patrik.

344
00:30:16,760 --> 00:30:20,760
<i>Tell us a bit about your book!</i>

345
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:23,200
<i>"Mom, Dad, Father." Is it that one?</i>

346
00:30:23,400 --> 00:30:28,120
<i>She hasn't read any of my books.</i>

347
00:30:57,640 --> 00:31:00,880
- Sheyma? Help me a bit here.
- Coming.

348
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:04,800
Damn, you girls are going for it!
This looks fucking great.

349
00:31:04,960 --> 00:31:07,760
Should we put this down here?
Is it too much or nice?

350
00:31:07,920 --> 00:31:10,200
- I think it's nice.
- This is really nice.

351
00:31:10,960 --> 00:31:13,200
- I think it's lovely.
- So fucking pretty.

352
00:31:13,360 --> 00:31:15,800
Are you wearing that
to the costume party?

353
00:31:16,040 --> 00:31:19,560
That's what I was thinking.
A little angel, maybe.

354
00:31:19,800 --> 00:31:22,720
What do you think, darling?
Is this too cheesy?

355
00:31:22,880 --> 00:31:24,520
- Cool.
- I think it's cool.

356
00:31:24,680 --> 00:31:25,720
It looks amazing.

357
00:31:25,880 --> 00:31:28,720
I want Helga to sew stuff
for the costume party.

358
00:31:28,880 --> 00:31:32,120
- Great idea.
- Right? Great for your brand.

359
00:31:32,280 --> 00:31:36,320
- There'll be good people there.
- I've got loads to do before Copenhagen.

360
00:31:36,480 --> 00:31:40,840
Yeah, okay. I've just put Vilma to bed.
So I thought maybe...

361
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:42,800
I need to finish up here.

362
00:31:42,960 --> 00:31:46,120
- I just wanted to say I'm off to bed.
- Good night.

363
00:31:46,280 --> 00:31:49,960
Yeah, sleep well.
I've started some new medication.

364
00:31:50,120 --> 00:31:54,000
It's some kind of anti-anxiety thing.
So I'm totally, like, chill.

365
00:31:55,400 --> 00:31:59,480
- That's great, honey.
- It's fucking great. It's thanks to you.

366
00:32:00,320 --> 00:32:04,440
I mean it. It's him, your new guy.

367
00:32:04,600 --> 00:32:10,080
Gabriel, Lena's new guy.
We really connected.

368
00:32:10,520 --> 00:32:12,840
We could really talk about everything.
Sleep well.

369
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:22,600
There we go!
I've activated your key card.

370
00:32:22,760 --> 00:32:25,040
Great, thank you so much!

371
00:32:26,280 --> 00:32:29,040
- Hi!
- Hi! I'd like to book a room.

372
00:32:29,200 --> 00:32:32,720
Do you have one at the top
with a view of the park?

373
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:05,640
You'll send the stuff then?

374
00:33:05,800 --> 00:33:09,560
Absolutely, I'll fix that.
See you tomorrow.

375
00:33:09,800 --> 00:33:12,200
- Thank you for today.
- Love you.

376
00:33:56,960 --> 00:34:00,840
<i>- Hi, Kristin.
- Hi, Gabriel. What are you up to?</i>

377
00:34:01,440 --> 00:34:04,800
<i>- Nothing special.
- I'm throwing a housewarming party.</i>

378
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:07,000
<i>Do you want to come?</i>

379
00:34:07,160 --> 00:34:11,240
<i>- That sounds nice.
- The door code is...</i>

380
00:34:11,400 --> 00:34:15,920
Actually, I forgot,
I've arranged to meet a friend.

381
00:34:16,080 --> 00:34:17,840
<i>- Unfortunately, I can't come.
- Okay.</i>

382
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:21,080
He's calling now,
I have to hang up.

383
00:34:21,240 --> 00:34:22,120
<i>- Yeah, see you.
- Bye.</i>

384
00:35:07,720 --> 00:35:12,760
<i>For me, beauty comes from the inside
and I want you...</i>

385
00:35:13,600 --> 00:35:14,760
What the f...

386
00:35:19,720 --> 00:35:24,120
<i>try to focus on glowing skin...</i>

387
00:35:27,400 --> 00:35:32,760
<i>I feel like that makes you both feel good
inside and outside. And then, I...</i>

388
00:36:32,080 --> 00:36:35,760
- Helga. Hi.
- Hi.

389
00:36:35,920 --> 00:36:37,560
What are you doing here?

390
00:36:38,320 --> 00:36:42,280
I'm just taking a little power walk.
What are you doing?

391
00:36:42,480 --> 00:36:46,640
Walking home.
I've had a few beers. Nice to see you.

392
00:36:46,800 --> 00:36:49,520
It's strange to run into you right now,

393
00:36:49,680 --> 00:36:55,400
because Patrik just said
that you gave him some new medication.

394
00:36:55,640 --> 00:36:59,520
And that you apparently really connected.

395
00:36:59,880 --> 00:37:05,240
Did he say that?
Good that he believed that.

396
00:37:05,400 --> 00:37:07,080
- I didn't say anything.
- What did you say then?

397
00:37:07,960 --> 00:37:10,680
- Nothing about that.
- Did he ask you to talk to me?

398
00:37:10,840 --> 00:37:14,280
- Did you two come up with a sick plan...
- No.

399
00:37:16,720 --> 00:37:18,560
Breathe on me.

400
00:37:19,080 --> 00:37:20,760
- What?
- Breathe on me.

401
00:37:22,680 --> 00:37:24,240
You don't smell like beer.

402
00:37:26,800 --> 00:37:29,720
- I don't know...
- Why are you so nervous?

403
00:37:29,880 --> 00:37:33,520
What the hell have you two been...
Did you tell him the things I told you?

404
00:37:33,680 --> 00:37:37,640
I have confidentiality, and I keep it.
I would never say anything about you.

405
00:37:38,240 --> 00:37:40,240
Yeah, I hope so.

406
00:37:42,000 --> 00:37:43,760
Do you know what he says about you?

407
00:37:46,400 --> 00:37:50,560
He says you're an addict
who lies to get painkillers.

408
00:37:50,720 --> 00:37:52,560
I didn't believe him.

409
00:37:53,880 --> 00:37:57,120
So I prescribed him medication
for your sake.

410
00:37:57,960 --> 00:37:59,080
Yes, it's true.

411
00:37:59,240 --> 00:38:04,240
It's anti-anxiety. He feels better from
it, but it makes him tired.

412
00:38:05,160 --> 00:38:08,840
Can I ask, did he fall
asleep early tonight?

413
00:38:11,120 --> 00:38:12,840
- Yes.
- Yes.

414
00:38:20,160 --> 00:38:22,160
I just want to...

415
00:38:23,120 --> 00:38:24,400
I'm sorry.

416
00:38:25,360 --> 00:38:28,920
I can get a bit paranoid sometimes.

417
00:38:29,080 --> 00:38:34,400
That's okay.
I just want to say that you can trust me.

418
00:38:35,360 --> 00:38:36,920
With anything.

419
00:38:39,600 --> 00:38:40,840
Yes.

420
00:38:43,200 --> 00:38:46,280
There actually is one thing I'd like to...

421
00:38:47,160 --> 00:38:49,280
A terrible thing.

422
00:38:49,560 --> 00:38:51,120
Helga!

423
00:38:52,320 --> 00:38:54,120
- Hey!
- Hi!

424
00:38:54,280 --> 00:38:57,680
- What the hell are you doing here?
- What are you doing here?

425
00:38:59,640 --> 00:39:02,840
- Is everything okay? Nice to see you.
- How are you?

426
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:05,240
I'm fine. Who is this?

427
00:39:05,440 --> 00:39:10,640
This is Martin.
He's my friend Felix's boyfriend.

428
00:39:11,400 --> 00:39:15,000
- You know Felix?
- No.

429
00:39:15,240 --> 00:39:20,680
Yes. This is Klas, and Klas is dating,

430
00:39:20,840 --> 00:39:25,400
or well, I guess he's with Olivia now,
who's Patrik's sister.

431
00:39:25,600 --> 00:39:27,960
But it's a secret,
so you can't tell anyone.

432
00:39:28,120 --> 00:39:29,600
If you do...

433
00:39:31,280 --> 00:39:35,440
- I'm actually meeting Olivia at Hommage.
- Now?

434
00:39:35,720 --> 00:39:38,200
I think she'd love it if you joined.

435
00:39:38,480 --> 00:39:42,200
Yeah, absolutely. Want to come, Martin?

436
00:39:42,760 --> 00:39:46,280
No, it's late. I have to go home to Felix.

437
00:39:47,440 --> 00:39:51,680
- It was nice meeting you.
- Bye. Say hi to Felix.

438
00:39:51,960 --> 00:39:54,120
She'll be so happy to see you.

439
00:39:54,280 --> 00:39:58,240
- I just need to... Just two minutes.
- Do it.

440
00:40:04,600 --> 00:40:08,560
I'm pregnant. I don't know what to...

441
00:40:08,720 --> 00:40:11,880
- Call me. You can trust me.
- Okay.

442
00:40:14,880 --> 00:40:16,800
- Hommage, then.
- Okay.

443
00:40:16,960 --> 00:40:22,920
- Great timing! And Olivia is there?
- Yes.

444
00:41:10,800 --> 00:41:13,960
Hi. I forgot my earphones.

445
00:41:14,120 --> 00:41:15,760
What are you doing?

446
00:41:16,600 --> 00:41:18,000
- What did you say?
- What are you doing?

447
00:41:20,640 --> 00:41:21,600
I...

448
00:41:23,160 --> 00:41:26,520
I wrote a note.

449
00:41:27,840 --> 00:41:28,960
A note?

450
00:41:30,040 --> 00:41:31,280
Yes, I...

451
00:41:33,480 --> 00:41:38,440
I'm a bit shy, as you may know.

452
00:41:39,120 --> 00:41:43,680
So I wrote a note
that I thought you'd find tomorrow.

453
00:41:44,480 --> 00:41:50,360
I'd really like to take you out to dinner.
I like you, Kristin.

454
00:41:53,720 --> 00:41:58,160
Okay. Like me as...? In what way?

455
00:41:58,320 --> 00:42:02,880
Like I noticed you've put your hair up
since we met at the rooftop bar.

456
00:42:03,040 --> 00:42:05,560
And that you invited me
to your party.

457
00:42:05,720 --> 00:42:08,920
And that you seem to enjoy my company.

458
00:42:09,920 --> 00:42:15,680
It really suits you, the hair.
Your eyes and cheekbones stand out.

459
00:42:15,960 --> 00:42:18,840
How about Friday evening?

460
00:42:23,120 --> 00:42:28,080
- I can't on Friday, but maybe Saturday?
- That sounds great. Lovely.

461
00:42:28,240 --> 00:42:30,400
- Okay.
- How nice.

462
00:42:31,680 --> 00:42:33,160
Okay.

463
00:42:40,280 --> 00:42:43,000
Why did you want to become a doctor?

464
00:42:43,760 --> 00:42:48,520
I found school easy.
It seemed like a sensible option.

465
00:42:50,800 --> 00:42:51,960
Answer honestly.

466
00:42:54,040 --> 00:42:58,240
I had good grades and...

467
00:42:58,880 --> 00:43:01,080
Yeah, and then?

468
00:43:01,240 --> 00:43:06,200
<i>- I don't think that's relevant.
- But I want to know.</i>

469
00:43:15,320 --> 00:43:21,120
Sometimes I think
I should have been something else.

470
00:43:23,040 --> 00:43:25,760
Yeah, it's tough to know what you want.

471
00:43:26,760 --> 00:43:28,360
What do you mean?

472
00:43:29,680 --> 00:43:34,360
- What does anyone want from their life?
- What do you want?

473
00:43:36,360 --> 00:43:38,080
With life?

474
00:43:42,360 --> 00:43:43,640
Love.

475
00:43:45,440 --> 00:43:49,680
Isn't that what it all comes down to
in the end? We want to be loved.

476
00:43:51,760 --> 00:43:54,560
It sounds simple, but...

477
00:43:55,640 --> 00:43:57,080
Have you got...?

478
00:43:58,800 --> 00:43:59,880
Yes.

479
00:44:04,560 --> 00:44:09,720
You take this first pill tonight.

480
00:44:10,200 --> 00:44:13,560
Then come to the practice on Saturday,
to get the second...

481
00:44:13,720 --> 00:44:16,120
No, it's Patrik's birthday on Saturday.

482
00:44:16,320 --> 00:44:20,120
The practice is empty then. We can't wait.
After 12 weeks, you'll need surgery.

483
00:44:20,280 --> 00:44:24,120
No, just give me the other pill,
and I'll sort it out.

484
00:44:24,280 --> 00:44:26,760
If anything goes wrong,
it's my responsibility.

485
00:44:26,920 --> 00:44:30,560
As your doctor. And as...

486
00:44:31,280 --> 00:44:34,080
...your friend.

487
00:44:38,360 --> 00:44:39,360
Okay.

488
00:44:59,200 --> 00:45:02,960
We're cowboys, okay?
We're rodeo cowboys!

489
00:45:33,920 --> 00:45:38,040
Little Mommy? Little Mommy.

490
00:45:45,960 --> 00:45:50,840
<i>Happy birthday to you
Happy birthday to you</i>

491
00:45:51,000 --> 00:45:56,440
<i>Happy birthday, dear Daddy
Happy birthday to you</i>

492
00:45:58,480 --> 00:46:01,520
- Wait! The candles. Happy birthday!
- Okay. Help me.

493
00:46:01,680 --> 00:46:04,080
Okay, one, two, three!

494
00:46:18,200 --> 00:46:19,560
Vilma!

495
00:46:21,360 --> 00:46:23,480
Vilma, come on now! We're leaving.

496
00:46:23,640 --> 00:46:29,320
- You too, darling. How are you?
- Not good, actually.

497
00:46:29,480 --> 00:46:33,800
- What do you mean?
- I don't know what it is. Not good.

498
00:46:34,240 --> 00:46:36,560
- You poor thing.
- I've been shivering all night.

499
00:46:36,720 --> 00:46:40,840
- What? You don't feel that hot.
- But I am hot.

500
00:46:41,080 --> 00:46:43,760
Okay. You're not just trying
to dodge the lunch?

501
00:46:43,920 --> 00:46:48,720
Patrik, please. Stop being suspicious,
I feel like I'm going to throw up.

502
00:46:48,880 --> 00:46:51,560
Poor thing. You know what?
Stay home and rest.

503
00:46:51,720 --> 00:46:56,720
We'll head off and see you tonight.
You'll be better by then.

504
00:46:56,960 --> 00:46:58,680
- I hope I am.
- You have to be!

505
00:46:58,840 --> 00:47:03,000
It's a party in my honor, and my queen
has to be there. Get some rest now. Vilma!

506
00:48:06,000 --> 00:48:10,600
- Dear friends, let's gather for a moment.
- Yes.

507
00:48:12,400 --> 00:48:18,000
My beloved son, and soon my director.

508
00:48:19,520 --> 00:48:24,120
Patrik will direct me in his new film.

509
00:48:24,520 --> 00:48:29,080
The book is becoming a film!
So now it's official.

510
00:48:34,520 --> 00:48:37,960
I'll be playing myself.

511
00:48:38,120 --> 00:48:42,680
It feels very strange
and almost a bit perverse.

512
00:48:42,840 --> 00:48:44,440
I understand that.

513
00:48:44,920 --> 00:48:49,520
- It's better than being written out.
- Yeah. Sorry, sis.

514
00:48:49,680 --> 00:48:54,240
If you don't want to win the Palme d'Or
and an Oscar... That's up to you.

515
00:48:54,400 --> 00:48:57,240
But your boyfriend will take care of that.

516
00:48:57,400 --> 00:48:58,960
I don't need you.

517
00:48:59,120 --> 00:49:01,960
- Cheers, everyone!
- Cheers!

518
00:49:02,640 --> 00:49:03,960
Cheers!

519
00:49:06,520 --> 00:49:10,480
What about your Danish brother?
Can he be in the film?

520
00:49:10,640 --> 00:49:13,560
We have to find a cameo role for you.

521
00:49:35,520 --> 00:49:36,480
<i>Repeat after me.</i>

522
00:49:36,640 --> 00:49:43,280
<i>Galumph, went the sweet little frog
one day</i>

523
00:49:43,520 --> 00:49:46,200
- You are the actor.
- Yes.

524
00:49:46,440 --> 00:49:52,240
Okay. I'm sitting here with Klas Recke,
Sweden's most sensitive and intense actor.

525
00:49:52,400 --> 00:49:55,640
He's going to play me, Patrik Gregorius,
in my upcoming film.

526
00:49:55,800 --> 00:49:58,240
What did you say
when I offered you the role?

527
00:49:58,400 --> 00:50:02,440
- I said, "You and I aren't alike at all."
- And what did I say?

528
00:50:02,600 --> 00:50:08,080
"If the Film Institute has a problem,
then they're racists and can go to hell."

529
00:50:09,440 --> 00:50:12,400
- Great. I'm so proud.
- Was it too much?

530
00:50:12,560 --> 00:50:16,080
No, it's perfect. You're amazing.
I'll tag you in this.

531
00:50:16,240 --> 00:50:22,840
Hey, does Helga have a gay friend
called Martin or Mattias?

532
00:50:23,000 --> 00:50:29,480
- Dark hair. Kind of handsome.
- No, no Martin. I know her friends. Why?

533
00:50:29,640 --> 00:50:35,280
Nah, never mind. I'm just rambling.
Oh wow, was that a little yawn?

534
00:50:35,440 --> 00:50:38,640
I'm on new meds, I'm completely wiped.
What's Sheyma doing here?

535
00:50:38,880 --> 00:50:43,120
- She's with Olivia, I think.
- Look, my brother's hitting on her.

536
00:50:43,280 --> 00:50:46,160
- He told me he's engaged.
- Okay?

537
00:50:46,320 --> 00:50:50,120
He's talking shit.
He's too much like me. One second.

538
00:50:50,360 --> 00:50:52,600
- Søren!
- Yeah?

539
00:50:54,680 --> 00:50:58,360
- Come on, I want to talk to you.
- I'll be back.

540
00:51:10,160 --> 00:51:12,080
Can I get another one?

541
00:51:12,640 --> 00:51:14,200
Helga, you can't.

542
00:51:14,480 --> 00:51:15,720
No...

543
00:51:18,360 --> 00:51:20,880
Could you come and sit here for a bit?

544
00:51:35,880 --> 00:51:38,000
I need to lie down.

545
00:51:48,560 --> 00:51:50,600
You're kind to me, Gabriel.

546
00:51:52,040 --> 00:51:54,280
You deserve to be treated that way.

547
00:51:57,560 --> 00:52:00,720
Patrik is kind too. He...

548
00:52:03,200 --> 00:52:07,480
- He puts up with me.
- You haven't done anything wrong.

549
00:52:09,120 --> 00:52:11,440
Then why am I here?

550
00:52:11,600 --> 00:52:15,360
It's his fault. Not yours.

551
00:52:19,560 --> 00:52:22,280
- Another one?
- Yeah, give me one more.

552
00:52:36,360 --> 00:52:38,560
- Wait, wait.
- Okay.

553
00:52:49,040 --> 00:52:51,280
- Sweetie, get Lena.
- What?

554
00:52:51,440 --> 00:52:52,360
Get Lena!

555
00:53:04,320 --> 00:53:05,480
Lena!

556
00:53:06,840 --> 00:53:12,560
- Here! Here! It's my heart!
- Calm down. Breathe.

557
00:53:18,080 --> 00:53:20,400
Do you love someone, Gabriel?

558
00:53:24,840 --> 00:53:29,600
I can tell you do
by the way your heart is beating.

559
00:53:31,040 --> 00:53:37,040
You're someone
it feels good to be loved by.

560
00:53:42,880 --> 00:53:44,720
Helga, you...

561
00:53:46,240 --> 00:53:48,720
- You could be free.
- No.

562
00:53:49,400 --> 00:53:52,640
You could. You could...

563
00:53:52,920 --> 00:53:55,320
I could never leave Patrik.

564
00:53:57,880 --> 00:54:02,480
All my friends in Sweden,
my daughter, my whole life...

565
00:54:02,640 --> 00:54:06,520
It all belongs to him.

566
00:54:08,640 --> 00:54:13,960
It sounds insane, but I sometimes think
it would be so much better if he was dead.

567
00:54:24,800 --> 00:54:29,240
It's going to be okay. I promise you.

568
00:54:29,400 --> 00:54:32,360
Everything will be fine.

569
00:54:53,440 --> 00:54:55,240
- You okay?
- Something is wrong.

570
00:54:55,400 --> 00:54:57,360
It's completely normal.

571
00:54:59,800 --> 00:55:01,960
What's happening to me?

572
00:55:05,840 --> 00:55:09,520
- You're fine. Is someone here?
- No, there's no one here, Lena.

573
00:55:09,680 --> 00:55:12,800
- We don't know that. Hello?
- There's no one here.

574
00:55:12,960 --> 00:55:18,840
Patrik, if you sit on the chair here
and just try to take it easy, breathe.

575
00:55:19,000 --> 00:55:23,000
- That won't help. It's my heart.
- I know it feels like that.

576
00:55:23,160 --> 00:55:25,680
I'm getting your medication.

577
00:55:33,320 --> 00:55:35,520
- Fuck, that's strange.
- What's strange?

578
00:55:35,680 --> 00:55:38,640
Kristin said it'd be here, but it isn't.

579
00:55:38,800 --> 00:55:42,440
- I'm going to throw up.
- Does it feel like that?

580
00:55:42,600 --> 00:55:43,680
Let's go to the bathroom.

581
00:55:43,840 --> 00:55:48,960
It's okay. Let's go to the bathroom.
Come on. Lean on me.

582
00:55:50,520 --> 00:55:54,000
- I'm going to throw up now.
- It's okay, go ahead.

583
00:55:54,160 --> 00:55:56,360
- Hello!
- Hi, what are you doing here?

584
00:55:56,520 --> 00:56:00,040
I'm prepping for this week's patients.
How are you, Patrik?

585
00:56:00,200 --> 00:56:03,720
- Not good. It's my heart.
- He's having a panic attack.

586
00:56:03,880 --> 00:56:09,680
Which is very strange, considering all the
anti-anxiety medication you've put him on.

587
00:56:09,840 --> 00:56:12,080
- Do you have the medicine cabinet key?
- No.

588
00:56:12,240 --> 00:56:14,720
- I don't want any sedatives.
- You need them.

589
00:56:14,880 --> 00:56:16,960
I don't want them!
Can't you just examine me?

590
00:56:17,120 --> 00:56:20,080
- I think you should examine him.
- Can't you just examine me?

591
00:56:20,240 --> 00:56:23,560
- No sedatives.
- I'll get the stethoscope. Just breathe.

592
00:56:23,720 --> 00:56:28,800
Do you want a sick bag, Patrik?
I'll get it from the bathroom now.

593
00:56:34,960 --> 00:56:37,080
- What do we do?
- Nothing. Wait here.

594
00:56:42,240 --> 00:56:45,480
Look what I found on the bathroom floor.
Kristin must have dropped it.

595
00:56:45,640 --> 00:56:48,040
- I'll get the meds.
- I'll listen.

596
00:56:49,000 --> 00:56:52,120
Here, Patrik. A sick bag.
Do you need to vomit?

597
00:56:53,040 --> 00:56:57,680
- Patrik, look at me. It's okay.
- Feel this.

598
00:56:57,840 --> 00:57:01,600
I'm going to listen to
your heart now. So just breathe.

599
00:57:01,760 --> 00:57:05,240
- Yes, I am.
- And be as quiet as you possibly can.

600
00:57:08,360 --> 00:57:12,080
What happened, Patrik? I won't tell Lena.
Why don't you want sedatives?

601
00:57:12,320 --> 00:57:14,160
Because I did a line at the party.

602
00:57:15,600 --> 00:57:18,600
I don't want to mix it with sedatives.
Am I going to die now?

603
00:57:18,760 --> 00:57:22,560
- I'm going to die! I am!
- No. Good thing I'm here.

604
00:57:22,720 --> 00:57:26,920
- Here I come with the meds.
- No, he just needs fresh air.

605
00:57:27,120 --> 00:57:29,480
- He says I'm not taking anything!
- Oh my God!

606
00:57:29,640 --> 00:57:33,520
- Help him. I'll turn the lights off.
- I just need to go to the bathroom.

607
00:57:34,080 --> 00:57:35,360
No!

608
00:57:36,280 --> 00:57:37,640
Wait!

609
00:57:39,320 --> 00:57:43,760
- What is it?
- Patrik's heart. We must go to the ER.

610
00:57:43,920 --> 00:57:46,120
- What do you mean?
- It's okay.

611
00:57:46,280 --> 00:57:50,080
- Cocaine overdose. Don't tell anyone.
- Okay.

612
00:57:50,520 --> 00:57:54,160
I'll pull the car around. If you take care
of Patrik, I'll just put on my shoes.

613
00:57:54,320 --> 00:57:57,080
- It's okay, Patrik.
- I told you.

614
00:57:57,240 --> 00:58:00,200
Come here, Patrik. It'll be fine.

615
00:58:17,480 --> 00:58:20,800
If we go to the ER now,
they'll find out about the cocaine.

616
00:58:20,960 --> 00:58:25,440
- We can't. We can't do that.
- They'll take a blood test and see it.

617
00:58:25,600 --> 00:58:29,120
We can't, Gabriel. It's going to be
all over the news. It'll be a scandal.

618
00:58:29,280 --> 00:58:32,960
- If you don't want to...
- It doesn't matter I'm going to die now.

619
00:58:33,120 --> 00:58:37,680
- You have to breathe now, Patrik. Focus.
- Yeah. No...

620
00:58:37,920 --> 00:58:42,240
- Patrik, look at me.
- I can't. I am.

621
00:58:43,320 --> 00:58:44,960
What are you doing?

622
00:58:52,480 --> 00:58:56,320
- Now breathe.
- I am breathing!

623
00:58:57,000 --> 00:58:59,480
- Out through your mouth.
- Yeah.

624
00:59:04,760 --> 00:59:07,920
You feel better now, right?
Can you feel your heart?

625
00:59:08,560 --> 00:59:10,280
Has it calmed down?

626
00:59:10,600 --> 00:59:15,320
Yeah, what the hell. What happened?
I'm fine.

627
00:59:16,200 --> 00:59:17,960
- That's insane.
- What?

628
00:59:18,120 --> 00:59:21,520
Your anxiety is so powerful, Patrik,
that I mistook it for a heart attack.

629
00:59:21,680 --> 00:59:26,560
But I can tell the danger has passed. You
don't need to go in. If you don't want to.

630
00:59:26,720 --> 00:59:29,400
No. No, forget it.

631
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:33,160
- That's crazy!
- I'm here now. Are you coming?

632
00:59:33,320 --> 00:59:36,320
It was a false alarm, Lena.
It's fine. I'm fine.

633
00:59:36,480 --> 00:59:40,240
- It was a panic attack. I apologize.
- Yeah, that's what I said.

634
00:59:40,480 --> 00:59:42,480
You saved me, Gabriel.

635
00:59:42,880 --> 00:59:46,640
- How are you? Are you okay?
- I'm fine. Sorry.

636
00:59:46,800 --> 00:59:50,920
- Go now. I'll go in and lock up.
- One second, Gabriel. Wait.

637
00:59:51,160 --> 00:59:54,000
Go to Mom's and kiss Vilma.
I'll go home and change.

638
00:59:54,160 --> 00:59:57,080
On one condition:
that you take it very easy tonight.

639
00:59:57,240 --> 01:00:00,240
- I mean very easy, okay?
- Yes. Sorry.

640
01:00:00,480 --> 01:00:03,000
- It's fine.
- I promise. Sorry.

641
01:00:03,160 --> 01:00:06,520
I'll take care of your mom and daughter.
Bye, Gabriel.

642
01:00:08,480 --> 01:00:10,120
- Thanks.
- I need to lock up.

643
01:00:10,320 --> 01:00:12,760
I'm coming with you. I can't be alone.

644
01:00:12,920 --> 01:00:16,000
- But go...
- I'm coming with you.

645
01:00:16,160 --> 01:00:18,560
I can't be alone. Okay?
Just a while.

646
01:00:18,720 --> 01:00:21,760
But we can't. I have to... You know what?

647
01:00:21,920 --> 01:00:25,760
Let's go to a bar.
Have a drink so you can relax.

648
01:00:25,920 --> 01:00:28,320
Are you kidding? A drink?

649
01:00:29,840 --> 01:00:32,400
That's brilliant. Of
course we're doing that.

650
01:00:32,560 --> 01:00:35,640
I'm reborn, for fuck's sake.
That has to be celebrated.

651
01:00:35,800 --> 01:00:39,160
But no bar.
I've got wine and liquor at home.

652
01:00:39,320 --> 01:00:41,800
- That won't work.
- It'll be great.

653
01:00:42,200 --> 01:00:44,560
Come on. Let's party!

654
01:00:53,120 --> 01:00:55,720
I'm alive, motherfucker!

655
01:01:05,760 --> 01:01:06,680
Gabbe!

656
01:01:10,200 --> 01:01:13,600
<i>We're on our way to your place.
It just happened, unplanned. Get out.</i>

657
01:01:13,760 --> 01:01:15,480
What the fuck?

658
01:01:20,840 --> 01:01:24,000
Gabriel, isn't life wonderful?

659
01:01:25,200 --> 01:01:28,480
I'm turning 35 today.
I'm surrounded by family.

660
01:01:28,640 --> 01:01:32,720
I have a career that gives me
artistic and spiritual fulfillment.

661
01:01:32,880 --> 01:01:36,200
A miracle of a daughter
and a beautiful wife.

662
01:01:36,360 --> 01:01:39,120
A damn beautiful wife, right?

663
01:01:42,800 --> 01:01:46,600
- Regarding Helga...
- What about her?

664
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:49,240
Well...

665
01:01:51,560 --> 01:01:55,200
Now that I've gotten to know you

666
01:01:55,360 --> 01:01:59,760
and the anxiety you're living with
a little better...

667
01:02:00,960 --> 01:02:01,880
What?

668
01:02:02,040 --> 01:02:05,120
I mean that you and Helga are both
A-type people.

669
01:02:05,280 --> 01:02:06,760
She's out walking.

670
01:02:08,000 --> 01:02:11,360
Walking? Constant fucking walking.
What happened to taking a taxi?

671
01:02:11,600 --> 01:02:15,440
- Helga and you...
- Forget Helga. Cheers!

672
01:02:15,600 --> 01:02:19,080
- Cheers to life and to you, Dr. Glas.
- Cheers.

673
01:02:20,320 --> 01:02:23,320
- You had a panic attack.
- No, it wasn't a panic attack.

674
01:02:23,480 --> 01:02:26,640
I've had a thousand of those.
This was something else.

675
01:02:26,800 --> 01:02:29,960
I felt death's cold hands on my shoulders.

676
01:02:30,120 --> 01:02:32,520
It's true. Everything went black.

677
01:02:33,560 --> 01:02:37,840
But then you came and put your hand on my
chest and pulled me back into the light.

678
01:02:38,080 --> 01:02:42,160
I don't give a damn whether it was medical
or not. I know what happened.

679
01:02:42,400 --> 01:02:44,680
I'm eternally grateful to you.

680
01:02:45,480 --> 01:02:48,640
My friend, the archangel Gabriel.

681
01:02:49,640 --> 01:02:53,000
- It was nothing.
- You don't say much.

682
01:02:57,040 --> 01:03:00,800
But you see me. You really see me.

683
01:03:01,040 --> 01:03:04,000
And I can see in your eyes
that you don't judge.

684
01:03:05,160 --> 01:03:06,520
It's beautiful.

685
01:03:06,680 --> 01:03:09,400
- This is okay, right?
- Yes.

686
01:03:11,200 --> 01:03:14,600
- Want one?
- No.

687
01:03:14,760 --> 01:03:18,880
- We really need to talk about this.
- I feel like I want to give you something.

688
01:03:21,240 --> 01:03:25,640
I know, here! Of course!
What do you think of this?

689
01:03:25,800 --> 01:03:29,240
It should fit you, right?
We've got more in the bedroom. Come.

690
01:03:29,400 --> 01:03:32,120
We're having a costume party tonight.

691
01:03:32,280 --> 01:03:36,440
I'm going as a king.
Or an angel or something.

692
01:03:36,600 --> 01:03:40,680
We got a ton from the stylist. Try
that one. Or one of these should fit.

693
01:03:40,840 --> 01:03:44,920
Tonight's going to be really twisted.
Lots of sex and drugs and stupidity.

694
01:03:45,080 --> 01:03:48,320
Try this one! This may suit you.

695
01:03:48,480 --> 01:03:53,160
What do you think? You're coming with us.
And you're going to keep an eye on Helga.

696
01:03:53,400 --> 01:03:56,160
- Am I coming?
- You were onto something with her.

697
01:03:56,320 --> 01:03:58,720
She's meeting another guy
just now, on her 'walk'.

698
01:03:58,880 --> 01:04:01,680
- Why do you think that?
- I feel it in my soul.

699
01:04:01,920 --> 01:04:04,240
Like I've got a sixth sense or something.

700
